<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Analyzing Graphs and Statements in Function Notation</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01023</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Analyzing Graphs and Statements in Function Notation</md:title>
    <md:uuid>ef35b2b7-133f-4c53-9044-247d1b37ed59</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="numbered-exercises" id="sect-00001"><title>Warm Up</title>
      <para id="para-00001">This graph shows the populations of Baltimore and Cleveland in the <m:math><m:msup><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mtext>th</m:mtext></m:msup></m:math> century. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>B</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> is the population of Baltimore in year t. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>C</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> is the population of Cleveland in year <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">
          <media alt="Line graph showing population trends from 1900 to 2010 for Baltimore (solid blue line) and Cleveland (dashed red line). Both cities peak in mid-1900s, then decline, with Baltimore maintaining a higher population throughout.">
            <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_13_02_01.svg"/>
          </media>
        
    </para>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00003">Estimate <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>B</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1930</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and explain what it means in this situation.</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00004">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00005"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>B</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1930</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> is about 800,000. It’s the population of Baltimore in 1930.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->

        <exercise id="_0efe13e0-f6d2-4d04-9fce-340a0254928c" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00002">
            <para id="para-00006">Which statement is true: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>B</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2000</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>≥</m:mo><m:mi>C</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2000</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> or <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>B</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2000</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>≤</m:mo><m:mi>C</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2000</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00002">
            <para id="para-00007">Answer: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>B</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2000</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>≥</m:mo><m:mi>C</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2000</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            
          </solution>
        </exercise>
 
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00009">Explain the reasoning for your response to question 2.</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00010">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00011">Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.
      On the graph, the point that represents <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>B</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2000</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> is located at a higher location than the point that represents <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>C</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2000</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> for each function.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->

        <exercise id="cef364e6-c465-409f-bab7-149701c9cf07" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00004">
            <para id="para-00012">Which statement is true: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>B</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1900</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>C</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1900</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> or <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>B</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1900</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>&gt;</m:mo><m:mi>C</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1900</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00004">
            <para id="para-00013">Answer: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>B</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1900</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>&gt;</m:mo><m:mi>C</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1900</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            
          </solution>
        </exercise>

      <!--Interaction End -->
      <exercise id="exer-00003">
        <problem id="prob-00005">
          <para id="para-00015">Explain the reasoning for your response to question 4.</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00005">
          <para id="para-00016">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00017">Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.
      The blue function representing Baltimore has a higher <emphasis effect="italics">y</emphasis>-value in 1900 than the red-dashed function representing Cleveland does.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00004">
        <problem id="prob-00006">
          <para id="para-00018">Were the two cities’ populations ever the same? If so, when?</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00006">
          <para id="para-00019">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00020">Yes. The populations were the same in roughly 1910 and 1943.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
    </section>
  </content></document>
